  - epidemiology
  - prevention theorem
  - proviral integration
abstract: >-
  Computational implementation of the Prevention Theorem, which formalizes
  HIV prevention as a mathematical boundary condition problem. The theorem
  establishes that post-exposure prophylaxis (PEP) can achieve true prevention
  (R₀(e) = 0) only when initiated within a finite biological window prior to
  irreversible proviral integration. For mucosal exposures, this window extends
  to approximately 72 hours; for parenteral exposures, it is compressed to
  12-24 hours.
